<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Truce of Andrusovo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1667">1667</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-polish-war-1654-1667">Russo-Polish War (1654–1667)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Truce of Andrusovo, agreed in January 1667 in a village near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a>, ended the Russo-Polish War of 1654–1667. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> ceded Smolensk and left-bank <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> to the Tsardom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, which also received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, nominally for two years, while right-bank Ukraine stayed Polish. The division of Ukraine along the Dnieper was confirmed by the Eternal Peace of 1686.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/truce-of-andrusovo.jpg" alt="Truce of Andrusovo" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Mathiasrex Maciej Szczepańczyk, based on layers of User:Halibutt · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Truce_of_Andrusovo_1667.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
